  "schema": 1,
  "about": "Modwerk's Model:Cycles OS 1.13 base, built by npm run machine:base -- model-cycles, all of it Modwerk's own source: the hook bus core/core.s (shared with the Digitakt II and the Rytm MKII), and core-mc/, the recipe, the OS's routines and data by name (fw.s) and ev_boot (boot.s). common holds the core's five sites (boot, ev_tick, ev_draw, ev_key, ev_enc), each named by its stock bytes' length and SHA-256. Modwerk adds ev_key_leds (base/key-leds.s), the key-LED frame, as the Digitakt II has it: one source, one site and its collection. Every base carries the link's part for musicians' units, as the Octatrack's does (base/link.c, LINK.md): its identity with the set identity, the audio load (base/load.c, load.s), the diagnostics log in the Octatrack's layout (base/diag.c) read through LOG, and the runtime loader (base/runtime.c, base/modules.c: the Octatrack's loader and upload controller from sdk/runtime/, wire frames in parts over the link), which loads modules to RAM on trial and keeps or undoes them without a reflash. The base keeps every site, export, import, table and subscription of the core-mc 0.3 release it replaces (reference), so whatever was built for that release links to it. A collection's number is its entry size in bytes (a handler's address), not a count: the linker puts every subscriber in the hook's table.",
